{
  "_comment": "The manifest every SDK sends, and when: an explicit publish replaces it (PUT /api/apps/v1/manifest); the automatic send merges into the one Wakeshift has (POST /api/apps/v1/manifest/merge), with only the settings the app published and its events: from a process that serves the app's tools (attach), on its first call about events; from any process, when Wakeshift answers an emit with unknown_event, after which it emits once more. A case with unknown_emits: the fake core answers that many emits (the first ones) with 404 {\"error\": {\"code\": \"unknown_event\", \"message\": \"no such event\"}}, and requests lists each emit too, as {\"method\": \"POST\", \"path\": \"/events/emit\"} (its body isn't checked). Each SDK's test runs each case against a fake core: it defines the sample events named in define (events-list.json's chat.message, game.turn and ci.run, whose manifest entries that file pins), runs the steps in order, and checks every request it made to /manifest or under it (method, path below /api/apps/v1, and body; a GET has no body) against requests. In a request's body, an event that's a string is that defined event's manifest entry; an object is listed as it is. The fake core answers a GET of /manifest with {\"description\": \"\"}, a PUT or merge with 200 and its body unless the step's answer says otherwise, and every other request with {\"matched\": 0, \"subscriptions\": 0, \"connected\": 0, \"forgotten\": false}. Steps: attach (attach to an MCP server, with no options), emit (chat.message, with emit's arguments and payload), status (chat.message's status, with emit's arguments: a call that only reads), forget_user (forget the user \"ada\": an app call about no event), publish (an explicit publish of the manifest given, answered with answer if set), define (one more sample event), fail_next (the next request to /manifest or under it answers 503 with {\"error\": {\"code\": \"unavailable\", \"message\": \"try again\"}}). A step with error must fail, its message containing that text; every other step must succeed.",
  "emit": {
    "event": "chat.message",
    "arguments": { "channel": "eng" },
    "payload": { "from": "ada", "text": "shipped it" }
  },
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "a process that serves the app's tools merges its defined events on its first call, once, with no settings",
      "define": ["chat.message", "game.turn"],
      "steps": [{ "attach": true }, { "emit": true }, { "emit": true }],
      "requests": [{ "method": "POST", "path": "/manifest/merge", "body": { "events": ["chat.message", "game.turn"] } }]
    },
    {
      "name": "a process that only emits sends no manifest while Wakeshift knows its events, even after a define",
      "define": ["chat.message"],
      "steps": [{ "emit": true }, { "define": "ci.run" }, { "emit": true }],
      "requests": []
    },
    {
      "name": "an emit Wakeshift doesn't know the event for, before attach: one merge of the defined events, no settings, then the emit again; the next emit sends nothing more",
      "define": ["chat.message", "game.turn"],
      "unknown_emits": 1,
      "steps": [{ "emit": true }, { "emit": true }],
      "requests": [
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/events/emit" },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/manifest/merge", "body": { "events": ["chat.message", "game.turn"] } },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/events/emit" },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/events/emit" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "after an unknown_event's merge, attach sends nothing more for the same events",
      "define": ["chat.message"],
      "unknown_emits": 1,
      "steps": [{ "emit": true }, { "attach": true }, { "emit": true }],
      "requests": [
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/events/emit" },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/manifest/merge", "body": { "events": ["chat.message"] } },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/events/emit" },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/events/emit" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "an unknown_event's merge carries the settings the app published, and only those",
      "define": ["chat.message"],
      "unknown_emits": 1,
      "steps": [
        { "publish": { "description": "Team chat for agents" }, "answer": { "status": 503, "body": { "error": { "code": "unavailable", "message": "try again" } } }, "error": "try again" },
        { "emit": true }
      ],
      "requests": [
        { "method": "PUT", "path": "/manifest", "body": { "description": "Team chat for agents", "events": ["chat.message"] } },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/events/emit" },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/manifest/merge", "body": { "description": "Team chat for agents", "events": ["chat.message"] } },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/events/emit" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "an event Wakeshift still doesn't know after the merge fails the emit, after one more try",
      "define": ["chat.message"],
      "unknown_emits": 99,
      "steps": [{ "emit": true, "error": "unknown_event" }],
      "requests": [
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/events/emit" },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/manifest/merge", "body": { "events": ["chat.message"] } },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/events/emit" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "an emit after attach merges first and gets no unknown_event: no second merge",
      "define": ["chat.message"],
      "unknown_emits": 0,
      "steps": [{ "attach": true }, { "emit": true }, { "emit": true }],
      "requests": [
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/manifest/merge", "body": { "events": ["chat.message"] } },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/events/emit" },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/events/emit" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "calls that only read, from a process that doesn't serve the app's tools, never send the manifest",
      "define": ["chat.message"],
      "steps": [{ "status": true }, { "forget_user": true }, { "status": true }],
      "requests": []
    },
    {
      "name": "a process with no events defined never sends the manifest",
      "define": [],
      "steps": [{ "forget_user": true }, { "forget_user": true }],
      "requests": []
    },
    {
      "name": "a status call from a process that serves the app's tools merges the events first, once",
      "define": ["chat.message"],
      "steps": [{ "attach": true }, { "status": true }, { "status": true }, { "emit": true }],
      "requests": [{ "method": "POST", "path": "/manifest/merge", "body": { "events": ["chat.message"] } }]
    },
    {
      "name": "nothing is sent before attach; the first call after it merges the events",
      "define": ["chat.message"],
      "steps": [{ "emit": true }, { "attach": true }, { "emit": true }],
      "requests": [{ "method": "POST", "path": "/manifest/merge", "body": { "events": ["chat.message"] } }]
    },
    {
      "name": "an event defined after attach: the next call merges again, with every defined event",
      "define": ["chat.message"],
      "steps": [{ "attach": true }, { "emit": true }, { "define": "ci.run" }, { "emit": true }],
      "requests": [
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/manifest/merge", "body": { "events": ["chat.message"] } },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/manifest/merge", "body": { "events": ["chat.message", "ci.run"] } }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "an explicit publish replaces the manifest with its own events, then the defined ones, and the next emit sends nothing more",
      "define": ["chat.message", "game.turn"],
      "steps": [
        { "attach": true },
        {
          "publish": {
            "description": "Team chat for agents",
            "agent": {
              "wake": [{ "pattern": "chat.*", "description": "Messages in your channels" }],
              "post": [{ "pattern": "chat.message", "description": "Your messages" }],
              "ttl_days": 30
            },
            "others_can_wake": true,
            "preapprove_tools": ["history", "post"],
            "events": [
              {
                "name": "deploy.done",
                "description": "A deploy finished.",
                "arguments": { "type": "object", "properties": {} },
                "payload": { "type": "object", "properties": {} },
                "topic": "ev/deploy.done"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        { "emit": true }
      ],
      "requests": [
        {
          "method": "PUT",
          "path": "/manifest",
          "body": {
            "description": "Team chat for agents",
            "agent": {
              "wake": [{ "pattern": "chat.*", "description": "Messages in your channels" }],
              "post": [{ "pattern": "chat.message", "description": "Your messages" }],
              "ttl_days": 30
            },
            "others_can_wake": true,
            "preapprove_tools": ["history", "post"],
            "events": [
              {
                "name": "deploy.done",
                "description": "A deploy finished.",
                "arguments": { "type": "object", "properties": {} },
                "payload": { "type": "object", "properties": {} },
                "topic": "ev/deploy.done"
              },
              "chat.message",
              "game.turn"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "an explicit publish from a process that only emits replaces the manifest",
      "define": ["chat.message"],
      "steps": [{ "publish": { "description": "Team chat for agents" } }, { "emit": true }],
      "requests": [{ "method": "PUT", "path": "/manifest", "body": { "description": "Team chat for agents", "events": ["chat.message"] } }]
    },
    {
      "name": "an event defined after an explicit publish: the automatic merge carries the published settings and every defined event",
      "define": ["chat.message"],
      "steps": [
        { "attach": true },
        {
          "publish": {
            "description": "Team chat for agents",
            "agent": { "wake": [{ "pattern": "chat.*", "description": "Messages in your channels" }], "post": [], "ttl_days": 30 },
            "others_can_wake": true,
            "preapprove_tools": ["history"]
          }
        },
        { "define": "ci.run" },
        { "emit": true }
      ],
      "requests": [
        {
          "method": "PUT",
          "path": "/manifest",
          "body": {
            "description": "Team chat for agents",
            "agent": { "wake": [{ "pattern": "chat.*", "description": "Messages in your channels" }], "post": [], "ttl_days": 30 },
            "others_can_wake": true,
            "preapprove_tools": ["history"],
            "events": ["chat.message"]
          }
        },
        {
          "method": "POST",
          "path": "/manifest/merge",
          "body": {
            "description": "Team chat for agents",
            "agent": { "wake": [{ "pattern": "chat.*", "description": "Messages in your channels" }], "post": [], "ttl_days": 30 },
            "others_can_wake": true,
            "preapprove_tools": ["history"],
            "events": ["chat.message", "ci.run"]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "an explicit publish that failed: the next call of a process that serves the app's tools merges the same settings",
      "define": ["chat.message"],
      "steps": [
        { "attach": true },
        {
          "publish": { "description": "Team chat for agents", "preapprove_tools": ["history"] },
          "answer": { "status": 503, "body": { "error": { "code": "unavailable", "message": "try again" } } },
          "error": "try again"
        },
        { "emit": true }
      ],
      "requests": [
        { "method": "PUT", "path": "/manifest", "body": { "description": "Team chat for agents", "preapprove_tools": ["history"], "events": ["chat.message"] } },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/manifest/merge", "body": { "description": "Team chat for agents", "preapprove_tools": ["history"], "events": ["chat.message"] } }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a failed automatic merge is tried again on the next call",
      "define": ["chat.message"],
      "steps": [{ "attach": true }, { "fail_next": true }, { "emit": true, "error": "try again" }, { "emit": true }],
      "requests": [
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/manifest/merge", "body": { "events": ["chat.message"] } },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/manifest/merge", "body": { "events": ["chat.message"] } }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a manifest listing a defined event is refused before anything is sent",
      "define": ["chat.message"],
      "steps": [
        {
          "publish": {
            "description": "Team chat for agents",
            "events": [{ "name": "chat.message", "description": "A message.", "topic": "ev/chat.message" }]
          },
          "error": "chat.message"
        }
      ],
      "requests": []
    },
    {
      "name": "an event defined after a publish that listed it: the automatic merge is refused",
      "define": ["chat.message"],
      "steps": [
        { "attach": true },
        {
          "publish": {
            "description": "Team chat for agents",
            "events": [{ "name": "ci.run", "description": "A CI run finished.", "topic": "ev/ci.run" }]
          }
        },
        { "define": "ci.run" },
        { "emit": true, "error": "ci.run" }
      ],
      "requests": [
        {
          "method": "PUT",
          "path": "/manifest",
          "body": {
            "description": "Team chat for agents",
            "events": [{ "name": "ci.run", "description": "A CI run finished.", "topic": "ev/ci.run" }, "chat.message"]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
